<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
The iOS, tvOS and macOS apps' keys the build settings cannot express; Xcode merges the generated ones
(GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE) into this file. It goes through the C preprocessor (apple/project.yml's INFOPLIST_PREPROCESS,
in traditional mode, where two slashes start no comment, so Sparkle's feed URL stays whole; its text never holds a C
comment opener, slash then star): the iOS app defines PLEZY_IOS, the tvOS app PLEZY_TVOS and the macOS app
PLEZY_MACOS, so each platform's own keys sit under its `#if`, and those of iPhone, iPad and Apple TV under
`#if !PLEZY_MACOS`.

App Transport Security: NSAllowsArbitraryLoads lets the shared core's HTTP client (the Ktor Darwin engine,
URLSession) and the Top Shelf's artwork reach media servers over plain HTTP, at home and on the internet alike, as
users enter them. It is the only ATS key: any of NSAllowsLocalNetworking, NSAllowsArbitraryLoadsForMedia or
NSAllowsArbitraryLoadsInWebContent beside it makes the system ignore it. mpv opens streams with FFmpeg's own HTTP
stack over BSD sockets, which ATS does not govern.

Files on iPhone and iPad (PLEZY_IOS): UIFileSharingEnabled and LSSupportsOpeningDocumentsInPlace show the app's
Documents folder in the Files app.

Background audio on iPhone and iPad only (PLEZY_IOS): picture in picture keeps the playback running while the app is
in the background, and music plays on with the screen locked. On tvOS the app is suspended when it leaves the screen.
The key is the plain UIBackgroundModes: the system's picture in picture reads only that one, and device-specific keys
(UIBackgroundModes~iphone) left the PiP button disabled on an iPhone while the simulators showed nothing wrong.

Languages: CFBundleLocalizations lists the interface languages (the files in shared/i18n); it makes the system
offer the per-app language setting (iOS, iPadOS, macOS) and follow the system language (tvOS). The app draws its
strings from the shared core, not from .lproj folders: the app reads the system's language list itself
(AppLaunch). The system's own prompts read the purpose strings (NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription, set in
apple/project.yml) from <locale>.lproj/InfoPlist.strings, which the build writes from the same i18n files.

Links: the `plezy` URL type, on iPhone, iPad, Apple TV and the Mac alike, opens `plezy://` links in the app
(PlezyApp's onOpenURL, RootSession.openUrl: the shared link queue), and in a DEBUG build's dev session
`plezy://dev-setting?<key>=<value>` changes a device setting while it runs (AppLaunch, for the UI tests); a dev
session hands every other link to its app's link queue. Its name is com.edde746.plezy, com.edde746.plezy.play on
Apple TV.

Casting: NSBonjourServices lists the DNS-SD service type the app browses for and advertises (_plezy-cast._tcp, the
shared core's CastDiscovery.SERVICE_TYPE) on iPhone, iPad, Apple TV and the Mac; iOS and tvOS refuse to browse for a
type not listed here.

Player apps on iPhone, iPad and Apple TV (ApplePlayerApps): LSApplicationQueriesSchemes lists the schemes of the player
apps looked for, so that `canOpenURL` can tell whether each is installed (it answers false for any scheme not listed
here): VLC's, Infuse's and SenPlayer's; Apple TV looks for VLC and Infuse only. The app's earlier releases declared
outplayer (iPhone, iPad) and youtube (Apple TV); they stay declared. The
Mac finds its players through Launch Services and PATH.

Apple TV (PLEZY_TVOS): the Siri Remote (MicroGamepad, several at once) and game controllers (DirectionalGamepad,
ExtendedGamepad, whose X opens a focused item's menu and whose shoulder buttons change a screen's tabs) move the focus
through the interface (GCSupportsControllerUserInteraction). CFBundleAlternateIcons names the
alternate app icons (apple/AlternateAppIcons-tvOS.xcassets), as an array: the asset catalog compiler writes only
iOS's dictionary form, which App Store Connect rejects for tvOS. The system keeps the icon a user chose by its name,
so the names never change. iPhone and iPad's alternates (apple/AlternateAppIcons-iOS.xcassets, the same names) are
declared by the asset catalog compiler (project.yml).

Appearance: no UIUserInterfaceStyle, so the app takes the system's appearance and follows it as it changes; the
theme picks it from the first frame on (ThemeState: Light, Dark, OLED and the accent palettes force theirs, System
follows the system's). The launch screen the system draws until the app's first frame (UILaunchScreen, generated by
the build) takes the system background colour: white in the light appearance, black in the dark one.

Sparkle on the Mac (Updates.swift): the feed is the appcast.xml on the repository's `appcast` branch, served by
jsDelivr, which the release workflow updates once a release is published. Every update must carry an EdDSA signature
from Plezy's own update key, whose private seed is the workflow's SPARKLE_PRIVATE_KEY secret; this is its public key.
SUEnableAutomaticChecks off: Sparkle neither checks on its own schedule nor asks whether it may; the app decides
when to check.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Where this build is distributed (ApplePlatform.flavor): project.yml's PLEZY_APPLE_FLAVOR. -->
	<key>PlezyFlavor</key>
	<string>$(PLEZY_APPLE_FLAVOR)</string>
	<key>CFBundleLocalizations</key>
	<array>
		<string>az</string>
		<string>bg</string>
		<string>da</string>
		<string>de</string>
		<string>en</string>
		<string>es</string>
		<string>fr</string>
		<string>hu</string>
		<string>it</string>
		<string>ja</string>
		<string>kk</string>
		<string>ko</string>
		<string>nb</string>
		<string>nl</string>
		<string>pl</string>
		<string>pt</string>
		<string>pt-PT</string>
		<string>ru</string>
		<string>sv</string>
		<string>tr</string>
		<string>uz</string>
		<string>zh</string>
		<string>zh-Hant</string>
	</array>
	<!-- App Transport Security: see above. -->
	<key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
	<dict>
		<key>NSAllowsArbitraryLoads</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
	<!-- Links: see above. -->
	<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleURLName</key>
#if PLEZY_TVOS
			<string>com.edde746.plezy.play</string>
#else
			<string>com.edde746.plezy</string>
#endif
			<key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
			<array>
				<string>plezy</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<!-- Casting: see above. -->
	<key>NSBonjourServices</key>
	<array>
		<string>_plezy-cast._tcp</string>
	</array>
#if PLEZY_IOS
	<!-- Picture in picture: see above. -->
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>audio</string>
	</array>
	<!-- Files: see above. -->
	<key>UIFileSharingEnabled</key>
	<true/>
	<key>LSSupportsOpeningDocumentsInPlace</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- ProMotion displays draw up to 120 frames a second. -->
	<key>CADisableMinimumFrameDurationOnPhone</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- A trackpad or mouse on an iPad sends pointer events, not touches. -->
	<key>UIApplicationSupportsIndirectInputEvents</key>
	<true/>
#endif
#if !PLEZY_MACOS
#if PLEZY_IOS
	<!-- Several scenes: iOS hands an app an external screen's scene (ExternalDisplay.swift) only when it supports
	     multiple scenes, which also lets iPadOS open more windows of the app; a playing video stays in the window that
	     shows it first (VideoSurfaceHost). -->
	<key>UIApplicationSceneManifest</key>
	<dict>
		<key>UIApplicationSupportsMultipleScenes</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
#else
	<!-- One window: the video surface can only live in one view hierarchy. -->
	<key>UIApplicationSceneManifest</key>
	<dict>
		<key>UIApplicationSupportsMultipleScenes</key>
		<false/>
	</dict>
#endif
#endif
	<!-- Player apps: see above. -->
#if PLEZY_IOS
	<key>LSApplicationQueriesSchemes</key>
	<array>
		<string>vlc</string>
		<string>infuse</string>
		<string>senplayer</string>
		<string>outplayer</string>
	</array>
#endif
#if PLEZY_TVOS
	<key>LSApplicationQueriesSchemes</key>
	<array>
		<string>infuse</string>
		<string>vlc</string>
		<string>youtube</string>
	</array>
	<!-- Apple TV: see above. -->
	<key>GCSupportedGameControllers</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>ProfileName</key>
			<string>MicroGamepad</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>ProfileName</key>
			<string>DirectionalGamepad</string>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>ProfileName</key>
			<string>ExtendedGamepad</string>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>GCSupportsControllerUserInteraction</key>
	<true/>
	<key>GCSupportsMultipleMicroGamepads</key>
	<true/>
	<key>UIRequiredDeviceCapabilities</key>
	<array>
		<string>arm64</string>
	</array>
	<key>CFBundleIcons</key>
	<dict>
		<key>CFBundleAlternateIcons</key>
		<array>
			<string>AppIcon-midnight</string>
			<string>AppIcon-ember</string>
			<string>AppIcon-paper</string>
			<string>AppIcon-oled</string>
			<string>AppIcon-line</string>
			<string>AppIcon-ocean</string>
			<string>AppIcon-ultraviolet</string>
			<string>AppIcon-matcha</string>
			<string>AppIcon-sunset</string>
			<string>AppIcon-gold</string>
			<string>AppIcon-titanium</string>
			<string>AppIcon-glass</string>
			<string>AppIcon-crt</string>
			<string>AppIcon-vhs</string>
			<string>AppIcon-synthwave</string>
			<string>AppIcon-pixel</string>
			<string>AppIcon-neon</string>
			<string>AppIcon-sticker</string>
			<string>AppIcon-ticket</string>
			<string>AppIcon-pop</string>
			<string>AppIcon-strata</string>
			<string>AppIcon-facet</string>
			<string>AppIcon-tilde</string>
		</array>
	</dict>
#endif
#if PLEZY_MACOS
	<!-- Sparkle: see above. -->
	<key>SUFeedURL</key>
	<string>https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/edde746/plezy@appcast/appcast.xml</string>
	<key>SUPublicEDKey</key>
	<string>q7t6eu1txRrqv1PeWDCRV95rFxnmD/D3GZWbUPMwUyU=</string>
	<key>SUEnableAutomaticChecks</key>
	<false/>
#endif
</dict>
</plist>
